1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,152
This technical test uses real commands and
synthetic sales data.

2
00:00:05,182 --> 00:00:10,394
The first calculation returns twelve thousand
across six monthly entries.

3
00:00:10,424 --> 00:00:15,715
Here is the exact change: June increases from
three thousand to forty five hundred.

4
00:00:15,745 --> 00:00:21,040
Running the calculation again produces a total
of thirteen thousand five hundred.

5
00:00:21,070 --> 00:00:26,366
We deliberately supply invalid input. The
program rejects it with an error.

6
00:00:26,396 --> 00:00:31,613
Restoring the original data returns the original
total. The result is reproducible.

7
00:00:31,643 --> 00:00:37,380
Sorting changes the order of the bars, while
preserving the underlying values.

8
00:00:37,410 --> 00:00:43,239
The filter keeps three months. Their combined
total is seven thousand five hundred.

9
00:00:43,269 --> 00:00:49,398
This structured output contains the same
calculation, ready for another tool to consume.

10
00:00:49,428 --> 00:00:54,416
A separate test checks the original app
calculations, invalid input and filtering.

11
00:00:54,446 --> 00:00:58,970
The production engine exposes three operations:
validate the timeline, render, and check
quality.

12
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:05,407
Fourteen tests pass here, including an actual
video render, decode and audio check.

13
00:01:05,437 --> 00:01:10,246
The encoder is FFmpeg. This footage replays a
real recorded terminal session.

14
00:01:10,276 --> 00:01:15,370
The source hashes preserve provenance. This
validates components, not a finished autonomous
channel.
